{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.\n\nInspected: Read configured recognition, bounded-height and lattice endpoints and their lattice, Lie-model, metric and height structures; matched recognition and lattice assertions, leaving metric-extension equivalence unclaimed.","content_sha256":"sha256:4581a6b5ae587f2477ec0e39e329c4fa4e327b6675d670db243fbe31c955ed9e","fingerprint":"sha256:1a5f352a755dc7de33a20c3779f491314371590759b010731dd3fedcf5b3b946","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:c3088158fa7dc55ad4c265ae58a75c2ef61dd04741e18bd0ba2045494e4fa965","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.PolycyclicRecognition.group_recognition"],"explanation":"The group_recognition declaration concludes virtual polycyclicity for a finitely generated group coarsely equivalent to a finitely generated virtually polycyclic group. This is the paper recognition theorem. The declaration additionally supplies a finite-index uniform-lattice realization, so this anchor covers only its first conjunct.","fingerprint":"sha256:b621a84827fe21836cf8a915ac5c3f6840631fa9ea3006a79ac3bb19d6f9076f","limitations":"The extra lattice realization is not asserted by this anchor alone.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026#thm:recognition","statement_sha256":"sha256:5a9587e59411a90093b9a2d10af9c70a46e22b9d0d37ffc7f7b5d20695d026cd"},{"declarations":["OAI.PolycyclicRecognition.lattice_recognition"],"explanation":"The lattice_recognition declaration takes a finite-covolume lattice in a simply connected solvable Lie group and a finitely generated coarsely equivalent group. It produces a finite-index subgroup isomorphic to a uniform lattice in another simply connected solvable Lie group. These are the hypotheses and conclusion of the paper lattice-recognition corollary.","fingerprint":"sha256:b20056747715d3b85aea5385e749f6002263f402b62ba0ea5260b994560aea02","limitations":"The separately configured bounded-height theorem uses an explicit compatible proper chain metric rather than the displayed Riemannian-metric hypothesis; that metric bridge is not certified here.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026#cor:lattice-recognition","statement_sha256":"sha256:25e915910b8a84e209995eee8f96caa63be9c6431fe039bff5be815e84ad9a3b"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/PolycyclicRecognition.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L10","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L18"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:PolycyclicRecognition","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/31ad5d09e1937eb35bb256bf.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/31ad